{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1138166-what-does-an-avatar-of-6-look-like","id":1138166,"title":"What does an Avatar of 6+ look like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-06T18:16:57-07:00","id":1138166,"title":"What does an Avatar of 6+ look like?","content":"In one of the books I remember a rule regarding Sendings where they absorb Avatar shards by crossing the Gauntlet and exposing themselves to the Avatar Storm. I've decided to allow that a Mage can surround himself in epherma he has specially attached to himself so that he can catch and slowly absorb the Shards, after which I will defer to the rules about raising your Avatar given in Ascencion. With that in mind, assuming that the game ever makes it past Arete 5, what does an Avatar rated 6+ act like? Will it possibly be more trouble than its worth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T04:33:40-07:00","id":1138273,"title":"","content":"Think of the difference between 4 and 5 Avatar and extrapolate from there.<br /> There are no hard and fast rules on this so just go with whatever feels most appropriate for the Mage in question.<br /> Perhaps a primordial avatar of an arch angel will begin to manifest holy symbology on all things around them.<br /> Perhaps a dynamic avatar would manifest in dreams, causing the Mage to sleepwalk to a different location whenever it pleased.<br /> <br /> Perhaps having an avatar so strong is actually a bigger liability than anything else, and may even lead one down the path of marauderdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T05:15:51-07:00","id":1138282,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I remember how Arcane 6+ can be a burden so I was thinking about how to have fun with Avatar. I'm also thinking you will need a Will that is 2 points higher than your Avatar rating in order to keep it under control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T08:21:18-07:00","id":1138326,"title":"","content":"Whatever it wants to.<br /> <br /> As a more serious answer, I think you should differentiate between a 'naturally occurring' Avatar 6+ and one that has grown to that size by absorbing Avatar fragments. You can graft random animal parts onto a shark until it is the size of a whale but what you end up with will be neither shark nor whale nor combination thereof (except by happenstance). So while your angelic Avatar could start manifesting more holy symbols it is more likely that it will manifest random and even incompatible ones. <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that the Avatar has to become unstable or mad, but each Avatar has had aeons to learn how to interact with conscious minds and this process adds a whole bunch of new methods it is likely unfamiliar with. Chances are it is going to look strange and fragmented from the outside.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T14:43:30-07:00","id":1138404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1138166-what-does-an-avatar-of-6-look-like?p=1138326#post1138326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever it wants to.<br /> <br /> As a more serious answer, I think you should differentiate between a 'naturally occurring' Avatar 6+ and one that has grown to that size by absorbing Avatar fragments.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still wonder how it's possible to get an Avatar Rating higher than 5, outside of pure ST fiat. The Shattered Avatar Merit only gets you up to 5 in M20 (which I think is not a nice choice given that it makes for good RP and risks).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T19:27:56-07:00","id":1138475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1138166-what-does-an-avatar-of-6-look-like?p=1138404#post1138404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still wonder how it's possible to get an Avatar Rating higher than 5, outside of pure ST fiat. The Shattered Avatar Merit only gets you up to 5 in M20 (which I think is not a nice choice given that it makes for good RP and risks).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I would allow for a quasi sending created by a Master of Spirit that attaches extensions of Epherma to you so you can absorb them like a Sending does. After that, role playing with Seekings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T15:38:38-07:00","id":1140661,"title":"","content":"Avatars of 6+ are in essence the &quot;gods&quot; of old realities (or essences that would be perceived as such by other beings). Whereas Avatars of 4-5 have a &quot;demi-god&quot; status (particularly if said Avatar is Primordial in nature), those of a greater-than-PC-rating are proportionally more-so. (By Revised's standings, metaphysically speaking, Avatars of 6-7 were proper &quot;demi-deities&quot; and/or lesser deities in terms of essential essence; those of 8+ were gods, proper, such as occurred when a particularly powerful archmage Euthanatos usurped the power (Avatar) of a goddess so as to achieve a deific standing of his own (giving him a Avatar: 8).<br /> <br /> Over the years of playing Mage since it came out, I've only ever seen 3 PCs achieve an Avatar of 6 or greater, and it was usually either setting/story-driven (in one case), or as a byproduct of a decade+ of storylines and incarnations spanning many thousands of years (starting from the pre-Elder Ages of more than 30k years ago, in one case, and the re-awakening over numerous incarnations of a Primordial Avatar that recalled/related existence outside of time/space altogether, having &quot;memories&quot; of the future and the past... in the latter case stemming back more than an &quot;impossible&quot; 14 billion years...). Using that as a benchmark, the occurrences of a PC Mage having an Avatar:6+ should, for the player, be the proverbial once-in-a-real life -time experience of gaming....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T01:46:55-07:00","id":1140741,"title":"","content":"avatars of rating 5 have been described as &quot;mountains&quot; whereas those of rating 1 as &quot;cats&quot; so that should give you an idea of how metaphysically big an avatar 6+ is. of course in mage the avatar rating has few tangible benefits outside of spending(and perhaps storing) more quint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T12:49:15-07:00","id":1142270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1138166-what-does-an-avatar-of-6-look-like?p=1140741#post1140741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . of course in mage the avatar rating has few tangible benefits outside of spending(and perhaps storing) more quint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1138166-what-does-an-avatar-of-6-look-like?p=1140741#post1140741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">avatars of rating 5 have been described as &amp;quot;mountains&amp;quot; whereas those of rating 1 as &amp;quot;cats&amp;quot; so that should give you an idea of how metaphysically big an avatar 6+ is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and rules in Guide to the Traditions that lets you roll Avatar+Intelligence every 3 months of training for experience points. Also, you can spend quint to lower the difficulty of that roll. It really helps to highlight how Magi with high Avatar ratings can be potential luminaries to their kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T14:04:41-07:00","id":1142295,"title":"","content":"An interesting thing about the Avatar rating is, that it does not even necessarily, fluff-wise, mean that you have a more powerful or older Avatar.<br /> I forgot which book it was in, but it is mentioned that low Avatar ratings can also mean that you have a quite powerful, downright ancient Avatar...but it is simply not investing much time and energy into you. An amusing thought, really.<br /> <br /> Either way, I think a higher Avatar rating *does* mean that the Avatar also potentially tends to be more of a part of the mage's life - be it helpful aid, guidance or terrorizing, which can have big benefits (or troubles) in a roleplayed way. That's where the primary strength of the Backgrounds lies, really, aside of the rather simple Quintessence mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T04:10:47-07:00","id":1142456,"title":"","content":"I once actually played a Progenitor/VE (Dual Convention merit, basically a progenitor who went to space after being confronted with extraterestrial anomalies) with Avatar rating 10. The Avatar took the form of a gigantic alien being that tormented the character with challenges. Mostly was contend to just talk like a supervillain now and then, but used quite god like plot device powers twice as far as I remember. Once procuring a lost artifact related to the lost city of Atlantis from god knows where into a highly secured VE facility in lockdown (causing the AI in charge of the place to be very confused as to how the fuck that was possible) and once more disabling (or straight up eating, really) a planet wide satelite defense grid.<br /> <br /> Personally I wouldn't allow PCs avatar ratings past 5 unless it serves the story in some fashion. The way to get them should either be at chargen (and oh boy what an avatar that is... who is in charge here?) or by doing similarily involved rituals as voormas did. I think just collecting some ephemera or avatar shards shouldn't be enough, the difference between levels 5 is more qualitative than quantitative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}